<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matvei Platov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1753–<a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matvei Platov was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> general who served as ataman of the Don Cossack Host from 1801 until his death. He fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, and in 1812 his Cossacks harried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s army during its retreat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, after which he campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novocherkassk">Novocherkassk</a> as the new Don capital in 1805.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matvei-platov.jpg" alt="Matvei Platov" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Dawe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Platov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
